/F1 11 Tf 72 594 Td () Tj
/F1 15 Tf 72 584 Td (Original Inspiration) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 562 Td () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 552 Td (Drew made a creamy Mexican street corn-style topping in bulk for a family taco bar. This) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 537 Td (version keeps that creamy corn-dish format while adding grilled corn, smoky char, warm) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 522 Td (spices, hot sauce, and optional Tajín.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 507 Td () Tj
/F1 15 Tf 72 497 Td (Ingredients) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 475 Td () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 465 Td (- 6 ears fresh corn) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 450 Td (- Mayonnaise, for brushing the corn and making the sauce) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 435 Td (- 2 knobs butter) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 420 Td (- Sour cream, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 405 Td (- Chili powder, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 390 Td (- Paprika, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 375 Td (- Cayenne pepper, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 360 Td (- Garlic powder, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 345 Td (- Black pepper, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 330 Td (- Hot sauce, to taste) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 315 Td (- Tajín, for topping, optional) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 300 Td () Tj
/F1 15 Tf 72 290 Td (Instructions) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 268 Td () Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 258 Td (1. Brush the corn with a light coating of mayonnaise.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 243 Td (2. Grill or smoke the corn at about 350°F for 15 to 20 minutes, rotating occasionally,) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 228 Td (until cooked and lightly charred.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 213 Td (3. Slice the kernels off the cobs.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 198 Td (4. Melt the butter in a pot over medium heat.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 183 Td (5. Add the corn kernels to the pot.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 168 Td (6. Season with black pepper, garlic powder, chili powder, paprika, and cayenne.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 153 Td (7. Cook until the corn is fragrant and warmed through.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 138 Td (8. Stir in mayonnaise and sour cream until the corn is creamy and reaches your preferred) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 123 Td (texture.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 108 Td (9. Add a squirt of hot sauce and cook, stirring occasionally, until hot.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 93 Td (10. Serve as a side, taco bar topping, or bed for taquitos.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 72 78 Td (11. Finish with Tajín if desired.) Tj
